# Netlify response headers. Lives in public/ so Vite copies it into dist/, the folder Netlify
# publishes.
#
# Who may show these pages inside a frame: Nhexa's own sites. Only Content-Security-Policy says
# it: X-Frame-Options can't list several sites (ALLOW-FROM is gone from browsers).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://nhexa.cl https://laruina.cl https://elumbral.cl https://terminalcore.cl https://terminalkiller.cl https://spectra.nhexa.cl https://spellcast.nhexa.cl https://havenstore.nhexa.cl https://streamby.nhexa.cl

# The OAuth consent screen is never framed, by anyone: a framed "Autorizar" button could be
# clicked unawares. Netlify applies every rule a path matches; if it joins both
# Content-Security-Policy values with a comma, those are two policies and the browser enforces
# both, so 'none' still wins. X-Frame-Options is set here only, so it's never two values.
/oauth/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
